From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: close the Tx queue stop/wake
 race

edma_port_xmit() stops a Tx queue when its ring runs out of descriptors
and relies on edma_tx_complete() to wake it again, but the two sides are
unsynchronized: the stop is neither ordered against, nor rechecked
after, the ring state it was based on.

  CPU2 (xmit, ring N)              CPU0 (Tx cmpl NAPI, ring N)
  ------------------------------   ---------------------------------
  edma_tx_ring_xmit() -> NO_DESC
                                   reap descriptors, write cons idx
                                   netif_tx_queue_stopped() -> false,
                                     no wake up
  netif_tx_stop_queue()

Ring N is now empty and its queue is stopped with nothing left to wake
it: the queue wedges permanently, which is the failure
e2599aafc2 ("qualcommbe: ppe: fix permanently stopped Tx queues") set
out to remove but only fixed for the wrong-CPU case.

Close the window the usual way: after stopping the queue, order the stop
against a fresh read of the ring's descriptor availability and wake the
queue again if descriptors did become available; on the completion side,
order the consumer index update against the read of the queue state.
Expose the availability re-read as edma_tx_ring_avail_desc(), which also
refreshes the ring's cached count, so the retried xmit sees it.

The stop path is enabled by default (tx_requeue_stop = 0), so every
build takes this path.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c
@@ -220,12 +220,30 @@ static netdev_tx_t edma_port_xmit(struct
 
 		if (unlikely(ret == EDMA_TX_FAIL_NO_DESC)) {
 			if (likely(!edma_ctx->tx_requeue_stop)) {
+				struct netdev_queue *nq;
+
 				cpu_id = smp_processor_id();
 				netdev_dbg(dev, "Stopping tx queue due to lack of tx descriptors\n");
 				u64_stats_update_begin(&stats->syncp);
 				++stats->tx_queue_stopped[cpu_id];
 				u64_stats_update_end(&stats->syncp);
-				netif_tx_stop_queue(netdev_get_tx_queue(dev, skbq));
+
+				nq = netdev_get_tx_queue(dev, skbq);
+				netif_tx_stop_queue(nq);
+
+				/* The Tx completion NAPI of this ring may have
+				 * freed the last descriptors just before the
+				 * queue was stopped, in which case it saw a
+				 * running queue and skipped the wake up,
+				 * leaving the queue stopped with an empty ring
+				 * and nothing left to wake it.  Order the stop
+				 * against a fresh read of the ring and undo it
+				 * if descriptors did become available.
+				 */
+				smp_mb();
+				if (edma_tx_ring_avail_desc(txdesc_ring))
+					netif_tx_wake_queue(nq);
+
 				return NETDEV_TX_BUSY;
 			}
 		}
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_tx.c
@@ -220,6 +220,13 @@ u32 edma_tx_complete(u32 work_to_do, str
 	 * other stopped queue stopped forever once its ring fills.
 	 */
 	if (unlikely(!edma_ctx->tx_requeue_stop)) {
+		/* Pairs with the barrier in edma_port_xmit(): the consumer
+		 * index written above has to be visible before the queue
+		 * state is read, so that a queue being stopped concurrently
+		 * with this completion is not missed here.
+		 */
+		smp_mb();
+
 		queue_id = (txcmpl_ring->id - edma_ctx->hw_info->txcmpl->ring_start) %
 			   num_possible_cpus();
 		nq = netdev_get_tx_queue(txcmpl_ring->napi.dev, queue_id);
@@ -666,6 +673,24 @@ static u32 edma_tx_avail_desc(struct edm
 }
 
 /**
+ * edma_tx_ring_avail_desc - Re-read the descriptor availability of a Tx ring.
+ * @txdesc_ring: Tx descriptor ring.
+ *
+ * Refresh the ring's cached descriptor count from the hardware consumer
+ * index and return it.  Called from the Tx path only, so the cached count
+ * stays serialized by the netdev queue that owns the ring.
+ *
+ * Return: Number of descriptors currently available in the ring.
+ */
+u32 edma_tx_ring_avail_desc(struct edma_txdesc_ring *txdesc_ring)
+{
+	txdesc_ring->avail_desc = edma_tx_avail_desc(txdesc_ring,
+						     txdesc_ring->prod_idx);
+
+	return txdesc_ring->avail_desc;
+}
+
+/**
  * edma_tx_ring_xmit - Transmit a packet.
  * @netdev: Netdevice.
  * @skb: Socket Buffer.
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_tx.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_tx.h
@@ -296,6 +296,7 @@ enum edma_tx_status edma_tx_ring_xmit(st
 				      struct sk_buff *skb,
 			       struct edma_txdesc_ring *txdesc_ring,
 			       struct edma_port_tx_stats *stats);
+u32 edma_tx_ring_avail_desc(struct edma_txdesc_ring *txdesc_ring);
 u32 edma_tx_complete(u32 work_to_do,
 		     struct edma_txcmpl_ring *txcmpl_ring);
 irqreturn_t edma_tx_handle_irq(int irq, void *ctx);
